---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Umbra — Built by One Developer"
	description="Umbra is built and maintained by a single developer. Here's what that means for speed, privacy, and testing."
	rawTitle
>
	<section class="section container prose about-page">
		<h1>
			Umbra is a small, local-first toolbox for the tools developers reach for every day — built to
			run entirely on your machine, with nothing else assumed.
		</h1>

		<p>
			<strong>It's fast because there's no browser bundled inside it.</strong> A native Rust core
			drives the app directly — unlike an Electron-style app, it doesn't ship its own copy of
			Chromium — so it opens and responds like a small program should.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>The Mac build is checked by Apple before you ever see it.</strong> Signed with a
			Developer ID certificate and notarized by Apple.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Nothing you use it for is sent anywhere.</strong> The app makes no network calls except
			one, disclosed — the check for a new version — and you can confirm it yourself with a network
			monitor while it runs.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Windows and Linux are labeled honestly, not oversold.</strong> They work, but they're
			tested less than the macOS build, and that's said plainly rather than implied otherwise.
		</p>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about-page {
		max-width: 38rem;
	}

	.about-page h1 {
		font-size: var(--type-h1);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
	}
</style>
